EVALUATION.md §7.2, §10.2: dereferencing a ref into a poisoned table stops the reader and
names the table, in an expect subject and in a test's own statement alike.
-- a/a.canon --
/// A.
package a

/// An item.
record Item {
  /// Its count.
  n: Int
}

local let zero: Int = 0

/// Items; poisoned by the division.
let items: table Item = {
  a { n: 1 / zero }
}

/// A ref into items.
let pick: ref items = a

test "an expect reading through the ref" {
  expect pick.n == 1
}

test "a statement reading through the ref" {
  let n = pick.n
  expect n == 1
}
-- outcomes.txt --
a "an expect reading through the ref": failed true, stopped false, broken false
  expect line 21: passed false (reads poisoned items)
a "a statement reading through the ref": failed true, stopped true, broken false, reads poisoned items at line 25

error[E4102]  a/a.canon:14:10
  items.a.n: division by zero

1 error, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
